# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-obp` package. We use operator backpropagation (OBP) to reduce the depth of a quantum circuit by absorbing trailing gates into the observable.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng gabay na ito ang isang minimal na gumaganang halimbawa ng package na `qiskit-addon-obp`. Gumagamit tayo ng operator backpropagation (OBP) para bawasan ang depth ng isang quantum circuit sa pamamagitan ng pagsipsip ng mga huling gate papunta sa observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An expectation value $\\langle O \\rangle = \\langle \\psi | U^\\dagger O U | \\psi \\rangle$ is unchanged if we peel a trailing block of gates off the circuit $U$ and conjugate the observable by it classically. OBP applies this repeatedly, evaluating part of the circuit classically so that only a shallower circuit runs on hardware. The price is that each absorbed gate can expand the observable into more Pauli terms, so the depth saved must be weighed against the growth of the observable.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang expectation value na $\\langle O \\rangle = \\langle \\psi | U^\\dagger O U | \\psi \\rangle$ ay hindi nagbabago kung aalisin natin ang huling bloke ng mga gate mula sa circuit na $U$ at i-conjugate nang classical ang observable gamit ito. Paulit-ulit itong ina-apply ng OBP, na kinakalkula nang classical ang bahagi ng circuit para mas mababaw na circuit na lang ang tumakbo sa hardware. Ang kapalit nito ay maaaring palawakin ng bawat sinipsip na gate ang observable sa mas maraming Pauli term, kaya dapat timbangin ang natipid na depth laban sa paglaki ng observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see examples of how to build realistic workflows with this tool and execute on quantum hardware, check out the tutorials on the IBM Quantum Platform ([OBP Tutorial](/tutorials/operator-back-propagation)).\n"
msgstr "Para makita ang mga halimbawa kung paano bumuo ng makatotohanang workflow gamit ang tool na ito at magpatakbo sa quantum hardware, tingnan ang mga tutorial sa IBM Quantum Platform ([OBP Tutorial](/tutorials/operator-back-propagation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare inputs for OBP {#prepare-inputs-for-obp}"
msgstr "Ihanda ang mga input para sa OBP {#prepare-inputs-for-obp}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "OBP takes as input a list of circuit slices and an observable. It backpropagates slices one at a time from the end of the circuit into the observable, reducing circuit depth at the cost of additional Pauli terms in the observable. Here we generate a time-evolution circuit for a 10-qubit Heisenberg model and slice it by gate type.\n"
msgstr "Ang input ng OBP ay isang listahan ng mga circuit slice at isang observable. Bina-backpropagate nito ang mga slice isa-isa mula sa dulo ng circuit papunta sa observable, na binabawasan ang circuit depth kapalit ng mas maraming Pauli term sa observable. Dito, gumagawa tayo ng time-evolution circuit para sa isang 10-qubit na Heisenberg model at hinihiwa ito ayon sa uri ng gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below we draw the original circuit, then the same circuit recombined with barriers marking the slice boundaries — each slice is a unit that can be absorbed into the observable in a single backpropagation step.\n"
msgstr "Sa ibaba, iginuguhit natin ang orihinal na circuit, tapos ang parehong circuit na muling pinagsama na may mga barrier na nagmamarka ng hangganan ng mga slice — ang bawat slice ay isang unit na maaaring sipsipin sa observable sa isang hakbang ng backpropagation.\n"

