# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce circuit depth with OBP {#reduce-circuit-depth-with-obp}"
msgstr "Bawasan ang circuit depth gamit ang OBP {#reduce-circuit-depth-with-obp}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We call `backpropagate` to absorb slices into the observable. The function returns the expanded observable, the circuit slices which were not propagated through, and metadata about the procedure.\n"
msgstr "Tinatawag natin ang `backpropagate` para sipsipin ang mga slice sa observable. Ibinabalik ng function ang pinalawak na observable, ang mga circuit slice na hindi napagdaanan ng propagation, at metadata tungkol sa proseso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Left unchecked, the observable can grow toward $2^n$ Pauli terms. The `operator_budget` caps this growth — here we allow at most 8 qubit-wise commuting groups, which roughly sets the number of shots required to evaluate the observable on the QPU. Backpropagation halts as soon as absorbing the next slice would exceed the budget, which is exactly what happens below: only 7 of the 18 slices are absorbed before the observable fills all 8 commuting groups and the procedure stops.\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi lilimitahan, maaaring lumaki ang observable hanggang $2^n$ na Pauli term. Nililimitahan ng `operator_budget` ang paglaking ito — dito, pinapayagan natin ang hanggang 8 qubit-wise commuting group, na halos nagtatakda ng bilang ng mga shot na kailangan para i-evaluate ang observable sa QPU. Humihinto ang backpropagation sa sandaling lalampas sa budget ang pagsipsip ng susunod na slice, na eksaktong nangyayari sa ibaba: 7 lang sa 18 slice ang nasipsip bago mapuno ng observable ang lahat ng 8 commuting group at huminto ang proseso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To push deeper into the circuit, the `truncation_error_budget` keyword argument to ``backpropagate`` can be used to drop small-coefficient Pauli terms from the observable as it grows. This dampens the growth of the observable in exchange for some error proportional to the magnitude of the Pauli terms being truncated. The two budgets are complementary and may be used together: `operator_budget` controls the *size* of the observable, while `truncation_error_budget` controls the *error* incurred by discarding terms.\n"
msgstr "Para mas makapasok pa sa circuit, magagamit ang keyword argument na `truncation_error_budget` sa ``backpropagate`` para alisin ang mga Pauli term na maliit ang coefficient mula sa observable habang lumalaki ito. Pinipigilan nito ang paglaki ng observable kapalit ng kaunting error na proporsyonal sa laki ng mga Pauli term na tina-truncate. Magkaagapay ang dalawang budget at maaaring gamitin nang magkasama: kinokontrol ng `operator_budget` ang *laki* ng observable, habang kinokontrol ng `truncation_error_budget` ang *error* na dulot ng pagtanggal ng mga term.\n"

